    <section>
        <h3>Answer 1</h3>
        <div class="question-box">What is virtual memory and what trade-off does it introduce?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p>It uses disk to extend usable memory beyond RAM, but disk access is slower, so performance can drop when swapping.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3>Answer 2</h3>
        <div class="question-box">Which scheduling approach uses a time slice (quantum)?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p><strong>Round Robin</strong> — each process runs for a fixed quantum before being pre-empted.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3>Answer 3</h3>
        <div class="question-box">Why are interrupts often more efficient than polling for rare events?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p>Because the CPU doesn’t waste time repeatedly checking; it reacts only when the event occurs.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

